## CQ-TT-01 | Label and Eraser tooltips use "color" and "labeled"
@group client
@commands Served client (`qrun.py client`): read the Label and Eraser tooltips with shift held
@pass Label: "Right-click with a dye: color the icon"; Eraser: "Right-click a labeled item in your inventory: remove its last label"; no "colour" or "labelled" line
@fails creativelabels jar older than the lang edit (rebuild `:creativeLabels:`)
do {"tooltip_text": "creativelabels:label", "shift": true, "reject": "colour"}
expect READ tooltip_text creativelabels:label \d+: .*color the icon
do {"tooltip_text": "creativelabels:eraser", "shift": true, "reject": "labelled"}
expect READ tooltip_text creativelabels:eraser \d+: .*Right-click a labeled item
## CQ-TT-02 | Oven heat lines say "fueled"
@group client
@commands Place an Oven on a stone block (no heat), open it: the status line; JEI on any baking recipe: the heat line
@pass Oven screen: "Not heated: needs fire, a lit campfire, lava, magma or a fueled blaze burner below (not a stove)"; JEI baking page: "... or a fueled blaze burner (not a stove)"; no "fuelled" (LOOK)
@fails creativedelight jar older than the lang edit (rebuild `:creativeDelight:`)
@draft no driver step opens a placed block's screen or a JEI category page by name yet; owner LOOK
## CQ-TT-03 | MCA gray eyes option
@group client
@commands MCA villager editor (or the player editor) with Creative Compat's extra eye colors: the eye color list
@pass the option reads "Gray Eyes", not `Grey Eyes` (LOOK)
@fails creativecompat jar older than the lang edit (rebuild `:creativeCompat:`)
@draft no driver step opens the MCA editor; owner LOOK
